# Instagram

Stage 1 loads `@efemer_flowers` and `@himmlhaus` into **`ingest_items`** (idempotent on `account:shortcode`). Then `KeywordIngest` → `MaterializePosts` (see `ingest.mdc`). Soft `kind` and invitations come from Gemini, not PHP heuristics.

**Production primary path is Playwright headless** (`deploy/instagram-headless-dump.py`) — GraphQL/Instaloader often hits `feedback_required` / 429. Cron twice daily (`0 6,18 * * *` UTC → `deploy/cron-instagram-incremental.sh`): headless dump (Archiver layout under `data/instagram/`) → `ImportInstagramDump` → `KeywordIngest` → `MaterializePosts`. Keyword + Materialize always run even if dump fails. Log: `~/efemer2/logs/cron-instagram.log`. Docker `instagram-archive` loop stays **off**. Needs `.secret/instagram.cookies.json` (or `instagram.session`) + `.venv-instagram` with Playwright Chromium.

## Session

Store Jan’s Instagram cookies in `.secret/` (rsynced on deploy) and `sessionid` in Secret Manager:

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Project | `efemer-456414` |
| Secret | `instagram-session-id` |
| Local session | `.secret/instagram.session` |
| Local cookies | `.secret/instagram.cookies.json` (preferred for headless) |

Refresh when Instagram checkpoints the session (update both files + GSM).

## Run (headless)

Production one-shot (same as cron):

```bash
cd ~/efemer2 && ./deploy/cron-instagram-incremental.sh
```

Local:

```bash
cd ~/Sites/efemer
mkdir -p data/instagram
tmp/instagram-venv/bin/python deploy/instagram-headless-dump.py \
  --root . --count 12 efemer_flowers himmlhaus
# or one post:
tmp/instagram-venv/bin/python deploy/instagram-headless-dump.py \
  --root . --shortcode DfHAP5XDXbN efemer_flowers

./bin/job jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.ImportInstagramDump -f
./bin/job jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.KeywordIngest -f
./bin/job jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.MaterializePosts -f
```

Fallback when GraphQL is not throttled: `deploy/instaloader-incremental.py`.

## Legacy archive API (avoid)

`RefreshInstagram` / `RefreshInstagramAccounts` hit the private archive API and 429 easily — **do not use for routine ingest**.
